 in TypeScript would help a lot. I'm sure there's a way to make your suggestion work, but it's certainly not easy, at least for me","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1773839570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1773841378","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/4947#issuecomment-1773841378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4947","id":1773841378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5puqvi","user":{"login":"ahkhanjani","id":72540492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTQwNDky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72540492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani","html_url":"https://github.com/ahkhanjani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahkhanjani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-10-21T16:07:55Z","updated_at":"2023-10-21T16:07:55Z","body":"> The current API has bad DX simply because it was the _only way_ I could figure out how to make it work with tRPC's existing internal types. Having partial type parameter inference in TypeScript would help a lot. I'm sure there's a way to make your suggestion work, but it's certainly not easy, at least for me\r\n\r\nI see. I will look into it and let you know if I can figure a way out. I'm totally unfamiliar with the tRPC source code so I may need to ask some questions later on Discord.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> There could also be an \"isolated middleware\" that takes it's own input, but doesn't expose them to the procedure. Its job is only to do some internal computation and add some values to the `ctx` object.\r\n\r\nHow about this by the way? Is this related to the same DX problem? Do you think we can have that?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1773841378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/comments/1773842138","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/issues/4947#issuecomment-1773842138","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/4947","id":1773842138,"node_id":"IC_kwDOELj1_s5puq7a","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/r